- F-320 **The code generator compiles a block's local functions as closures, the group recursive and mutually recursive without a mutable cell.** Each local function of a [-`LetFn`-]{+block+} is a closure class made as a function [-expression's (`forFnExpr`),-]{+expression's,+} bound under its name in the block's environment, so a call of it and its use as a value go through the closure; it reaches itself as its own `this` and each sibling through a field of its class that the block sets once, after the whole group is made and before the body runs [-(`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java`, `forLetFn`, `localFunctionClosure`, `localFunctionOrNull`).-]{+(`compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java`).+} It refuses three forms that the specification allows, each after the checker passes the program, with its own message: a local function with static parameters of its own, two of one name in a block, and the `atomic` modifier (row 304); a varargs one stops at 'Can't compile VarArgs yet' (row 624). Under the switch-over's [-setting-]{+setting, measured once,+} all nine of the library's declarations that stopped at 'Can't compile LetFn' emit (F-34). Gated by `compiler_tests/LocalFunctionCallCompiled`, `LocalFunctionValueCompiled`, `LocalFunctionRecursiveCompiled`, `LocalFunctionCaptureCompiled` and `LocalFunctionGenericContextCompiled`, their `tests/LocalFunction*Walk` guards, and `XXXLocalFunctionGenericCompiled`, `XXXLocalFunctionOverloadedCompiled` and `XXXLocalFunctionAtomicCompiled`. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-codegen-local-functions/REPORT.md` sections 1 and 5.
- F-321 **Against the interpreter's prelude the checker reads the whole helper class that a binding names, so [-the one library cannot bind-]{+a binding that names+} a helper of [-`nativeHelpers/systemOps`.**-]{+`nativeHelpers/systemOps` stops its component there.**+} `systemOps.getArgs` answers an [-`FStringVector` (`ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/nativeHelpers/systemOps.java:29`),-]{+`FStringVector`,+} which `NamingCzar` maps to [-`FortressBuiltin.StringVector` (`compiler/NamingCzar.java:339-340`),-]{+`FortressBuiltin.StringVector`,+} a type that the interpreter's `FortressBuiltin` does not declare, so a component whose binding names any `systemOps` helper stops: 'FortressBuiltin.StringVector is undefined.' (row [-895). So-]{+895, which gives+} the [-one library binds-]{+code's lines). So a binding can name+} only {+a+} helper [-classes-]{+class+} all of whose methods map to [-its-]{+the one library's+} types; `FlatString`'s line separator names `stringOps.lineSeparator` for this reason. `System`'s `getEnvironment` and `getProperty` name `systemOps`, and neither stage reads `System`, so [-they will stop-]{+`System` stops+} wherever the checker reads it. No test checks it: the compiled tests check against the compiler's prelude, which declares `StringVector`. [-Shown-]{+Observed once,+} by the distance stage [-with-]{+on `19e9dbda5`, where+} `Library/FlatString.fss`'s `natLineSeparator` [-naming-]{+named+} `systemOps.lineSeparator`:[-'FortressBuiltin.StringVector is undefined.',-] 'File FlatString.fss has 1 error.'. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-string-natives/REPORT.md`, "A site that came, and went".
{+- F-322 **The compiled checker reads a helper's Java `String` parameter as the one library's `String`, a parameter that walk refuses at load, so the count and distance stages pass a binding that walk refuses.** In walk's world the checker reads a helper's Java types as the one library's (F-298), and its table maps a Java `String` to `String` (`compiler/NamingCzar.java`, `oneLibraryForeignJavaTranslations`). Walk refuses a helper parameter declared `String`, since a Java `String` cannot carry a string that is not flat (F-299). The two readings differ, and this bears on the design of the switch-over, where the compiled checker reads the one library's bindings. Read in the code. Detail: `compile-ladder/rung-string-natives/REPORT.md`, "Decisions", item 2; `reviews/string-natives-2026-11-05.md`.+}

